<title>INDIA: INDIA'S UNITED FRONT PANEL BEGINS MEETING.</title>
<headline>INDIA'S UNITED FRONT PANEL BEGINS MEETING.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The decision-making Steering Committee of India's ruling United Front on Wednesday began a meeting at which it was expected to discuss oil prices, officials said.</p>
<p>Prime Minister Inder Kumar Gujral, who had been delayed by nearly 90 minutes by other appointments, arrived at the site of the meeting, which began at about 8:25 p.m. (1455 GMT).</p>
<p>-- New Delhi Newsroom (91) 11-301-2024; Fax (91) 11-301-4043</p>
